---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { PLACEHOLDER, business, telHref } from "../data/business";
import { buildWhatsAppUrl } from "../lib/quote";

const whatsappHref = buildWhatsAppUrl(business.whatsapp, `Hi ${business.ownerFirstName}, please delete the messages about my quote.`);
const provider = PLACEHOLDER;
const email: string = business.email;
const headingClass = "mt-10 text-2xl tracking-tight md:text-3xl";
const paragraphClass = "mt-4 max-w-prose";
const linkClass = "inline-flex min-h-tap items-center font-semibold";
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${business.name}`}
  description={`How ${business.name} handles the details you send through the quote form, WhatsApp or phone, and how to ask for them to be deleted.`}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 md:px-8 md:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl tracking-tight md:text-6xl">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-lg">
      This page explains what happens to the details you give when you ask {business.owner} of {business.name} for a quote.
    </p>

    <h2 class={headingClass}>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p class={paragraphClass}>
      {business.name} is {business.owner}, a sole trader. He is responsible for the details you send him. You can reach him
      on <a href={telHref} class={linkClass}>{business.phone.display}</a>, on
      <a href={whatsappHref} class={linkClass}>WhatsApp</a>
      {
        email === PLACEHOLDER ? (
          <span>or by email at {PLACEHOLDER}.</span>
        ) : (
          <span>
            or by email at <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class={linkClass}>{email}</a>.
          </span>
        )
      }
    </p>

    <h2 class={headingClass}>What the quote form collects</h2>
    <p class={paragraphClass}>
      The quote form asks for your name, phone number, postcode, the service you need and a description of the job. It is
      only used so {business.ownerFirstName} can reply to you about that job. The site has no accounts and does not use
      cookies or analytics.
    </p>

    <h2 class={headingClass}>"Send request"</h2>
    <p class={paragraphClass}>
      When you press "Send request", your browser sends the form details to the site's Azure Function, a small program run
      by Microsoft Azure, which hosts this website. The Function checks the details and passes them through a messaging
      service ({provider}) to {business.ownerFirstName}'s WhatsApp, where they arrive as a message.
    </p>
    <p class={paragraphClass}>
      The site does not store your details. The Function forwards the message and keeps no copy, and nothing is logged
      beyond the standard request information Azure records for any website it hosts. The messaging service ({provider})
      handles the message on its way to {business.ownerFirstName} under its own terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class={headingClass}>"Message Darren on WhatsApp"</h2>
    <p class={paragraphClass}>
      The "Message Darren on WhatsApp" button opens your own WhatsApp with the message written out for you. Nothing is sent
      until you press Send in WhatsApp, and the message goes directly from your own WhatsApp to {business.ownerFirstName},
      not through this site. WhatsApp's own privacy terms apply to that conversation. The same is true if you text or call
      him from the links on this site: those go through your own phone.
    </p>

    <h2 class={headingClass}>Deleting a conversation</h2>
    <p class={paragraphClass}>
      Your details stay in {business.ownerFirstName}'s WhatsApp or text messages, and on your own phone if you used the
      WhatsApp button. To ask him to delete the conversation about your quote, call him on
      <a href={telHref} class={linkClass}>{business.phone.display}</a> or send him a
      <a href={whatsappHref} class={linkClass}>WhatsApp message</a> asking for it to be deleted. You can delete your own
      copy in WhatsApp or your messages app at any time.
    </p>

    <h2 class={headingClass}>Your rights</h2>
    <p class={paragraphClass}>
      Under UK data protection law you can ask to see, correct or delete the details {business.ownerFirstName} holds about
      you. If you are unhappy with how they are handled, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
